<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Punakha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1910</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punakha">Punakha</a> was signed in January 1910 between Bhutan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> doubled Bhutan's annual subsidy and promised not to interfere in its internal affairs, while Bhutan agreed to be guided by Britain in its external relations. The treaty secured British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s northern frontier against Chinese influence, and its terms were largely carried over into Bhutan's 1949 treaty with independent India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-punakha.jpg" alt="Treaty of Punakha" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Technopilgrim at English Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PunakhaDzong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
